# rotate-tick.env.local.example — operator env for the ROTATION TICK's launchd
# agent. Copy to rotate-tick.env.local (same dir; GITIGNORED — it carries
# machine-local paths and arming decisions), edit, then re-render + reload:
#
#     SWARM_HOME=/path/to/qofi-claude-engineering bin/swarm-launchd-install.sh
#
# Every KEY=value line here is merged into com.qofi.swarm-rotate-tick.plist's
# EnvironmentVariables at render time (bin/swarm-launchd-install.sh — see its
# header for the format/validation rules). Values are taken LITERALLY: no shell
# quoting or expansion happens here; a "$1" in a value stays a literal "$1" for
# the consuming script's `sh -c` invocation to expand. The template owns
# SWARM_HOME / CLAUDE_PROJECTS_DIR / SWARM_STALE_SECONDS / SWARM_TMUX_BIN —
# re-declaring those here is a render error.
#
# THE ARMING MODEL. The committed template deliberately ships UNARMED: without
# SWARM_CREDSWAP_CMD the tick's actuator (swarm-rotate.sh) REFUSES a live swap.
# This file is the "operator adds it out-of-band" channel the template comment
# refers to. Delete the file and re-render to disarm (reverts byte-identical).

# ── CALIBRATION GATE (do NOT skip to live) ───────────────────────────────────
# 1 = render the tick with --observe: each tick LOGS burn-vs-budget + the real
# limit signal to ~/.config/swarm/rotate-tick.log and rotates NOTHING. Run the
# observe→calibrate→enable sequence (PROJECT_SPEC §10, "Rotation hardening")
# before flipping to 0. Consumed by the installer; never lands in the plist.
SWARM_TICK_OBSERVE=1

# ── THE ACTUATOR ARMING ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The credential-swap hook. With the user-assisted login relay, wire the script
# BARE — NO "$1" suffix (unlike the keychain adapter): the relay's positional
# arg is a SWARM name, not an account handle; the account CHOICE happens in the
# operator's browser. The relay diagnoses the "$1" miswiring loudly if present.
#SWARM_CREDSWAP_CMD=/path/to/qofi-claude-engineering/bin/swarm-login-relay.sh

# Rotation threshold: NEAR fires when either window's used_pct >= this.
#SWARM_ROTATE_THRESHOLD_PCT=95

# The account ring. swarm-rotate refuses (exit 2) on an empty ring, so at least
# two handles are required — but under the LOGIN-RELAY model the handles are
# NOMINAL: they drive ring math and logging only; they do NOT select the
# credential (your browser login does). Keep a simple two-handle ring.
#SWARM_ACCOUNTS=max-a max-b

# Checkpoint hook (commit+push each repo before a rotation). This one DOES need
# the literal "$1": swarm-rotate invokes hooks as `sh -c "$hook" _ <repo>`, so
# the hook string itself must forward $1 (swarm-checkpoint.sh's documented
# wiring). The quotes/$ are stored literally and XML-escaped automatically.
#SWARM_CHECKPOINT_CMD=/path/to/qofi-claude-engineering/bin/swarm-checkpoint.sh "$1"

# ── THE USAGE DETECTOR (burn proxy) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The poller's probe. The ccusage adapter derives used_pct from YOUR token
# budgets (below) — it is a burn proxy, not Anthropic's real cap %.
#SWARM_USAGE_PROBE=bash /path/to/qofi-claude-engineering/bin/swarm-usage-adapter-ccusage.sh

# launchd's PATH is minimal (/usr/bin:/bin:...): `ccusage` and `npx` are NOT
# findable, and npx additionally needs `node` on PATH. Point the adapter at a
# self-contained absolute invocation — bunx is a single binary and works from
# a bare PATH:
#SWARM_CCUSAGE_CMD=/Users/<you>/.bun/bin/bunx ccusage

# Token budgets = what YOU treat as 100% of each window (REQUIRED by the
# adapter — without them it fails safe and every tick logs verdict=UNKNOWN,
# which makes observe mode useless). Start with a seed estimated from your own
# ccusage history, then CALIBRATE: compare the observe log's proxy verdict
# against real_signal and tune until NEAR fires shortly BEFORE the real limit.
#SWARM_5H_TOKEN_BUDGET=200000000
#SWARM_WEEKLY_TOKEN_BUDGET=2000000000

# ── OPTIONAL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Escalation hook for ring exhaustion (every account capped).
#SWARM_ATTENTION_CMD=notify-ops "$1"
# Make the REAL pane limit signal the authoritative hard stop (burn proxy stays
# the NEAR early warning):
#SWARM_POLL_CMD=/path/to/qofi-claude-engineering/bin/swarm-limit-detect.sh --or-poll
